{"resource":{"id":"rust-best-practices","title":"Rust — Best Practices","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Intermediate","readingTime":"16 min","pages":18,"lastUpdated":"June 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555949963-aa79dcee981c?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"Professional Rust conventions: project layout, ownership guidelines, error handling, concurrency, testing, docs, logging, performance, and production hygiene."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Coding Conventions"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Project Organization"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Ownership Guidelines"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Error Handling"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Concurrency"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Testing"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Documentation"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Logging & Tracing"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Performance"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Production Readiness"},{"id":"flow","label":"Flowchart"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary & Key Takeaways"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust — Common Mistakes","tag":"Programming","time":"14 min"},{"title":"Rust — Project Guide","tag":"Programming","time":"17 min"},{"title":"Rust — Advanced Concepts","tag":"Programming","time":"31 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Write idiomatic Rust that reviewers love.</li>\n          <li>Adopt production-grade patterns from day one.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Coding Conventions</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><code>cargo fmt</code> + <code>clippy -D warnings</code> in CI.</li>\n          <li>Snake_case for functions, CamelCase for types.</li>\n          <li>Prefer <code>&amp;str</code> parameters over <code>String</code>.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517694712202-14dd9538aa97?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Formatting + linting is non-negotiable.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Project Organization</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Workspaces for large repos, one binary per deployable, keep <code>lib.rs</code> focused on public API.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Ownership Guidelines</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Borrow by default, own only when necessary.</li>\n          <li>Avoid <code>.clone()</code> unless profiling justifies it.</li>\n          <li>Return owned types; accept references.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Error Handling</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Library crates: <code>thiserror</code> with typed variants. Binary crates: <code>anyhow</code> with contextual <code>.with_context()</code>.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>use anyhow::Context;\nfs::read(path).with_context(|| format!(&quot;reading {path:?}&quot;))?;</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Concurrency</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Prefer channels over shared mutable state.</li>\n          <li>Bound your queues.</li>\n          <li>Never block Tokio's runtime — use <code>spawn_blocking</code>.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Testing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Unit → integration → property tests. Use <code>#[should_panic]</code> sparingly; prefer <code>Result</code>-returning tests.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Documentation</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Every public item gets a rustdoc comment. Include <code>```</code> doctests for examples.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Logging &amp; Tracing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Use <code>tracing</code>. Assign spans per request; emit structured fields, not concatenated strings.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Performance</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr class=\"border-b\"><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Do</th><th class=\"p-2 text-left\">Avoid</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\">Iterator chains</td><td class=\"p-2\">Index-loops with bounds checks</td></tr>\n            <tr class=\"border-b\"><td class=\"p-2\"><code>Vec::with_capacity</code></td><td class=\"p-2\">Repeated growth</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"p-2\">LTO + <code>codegen-units = 1</code> for release</td><td class=\"p-2\">Debug builds in prod</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Measure, then optimize. Micro-tuning without profiling is noise.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Production Readiness</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Health + readiness endpoints.</li>\n          <li>Structured JSON logs.</li>\n          <li>Graceful shutdown on SIGTERM.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"flow\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Flowchart</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>edit → fmt → clippy → test → doc → PR → CI green → merge</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Using <code>unwrap()</code> in library code.</li>\n          <li>Ignoring compiler warnings.</li>\n          <li>Mixing runtimes (async-std + Tokio).</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Tip</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Convert warnings into errors in CI.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Great Rust code is boring: formatted, linted, well-typed errors, small APIs, and continuous measurement.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Should I use nightly?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Only for isolated experiments; ship on stable.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>anyhow or thiserror?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Libraries: thiserror. Binaries: anyhow.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Reflects community norms current as of 2026.</p>\n      </div></section>"}